  data:  # 2ecd
    kind: invariant  # 2ecd
    title: "Per-pass timer and file-counter not updated for passes that consume the intermediate representation"  # 2ecd
    status: violated  # 2ecd
    priority: 1  # 2ecd
    parent:  # 2ecd
    tags:  # 2ecd
    - dogfood_corpus_20260528  # 2ecd
    - dogfood_integrated  # 2ecd
    - dogfood_severity_significant  # 2ecd
    isbefore: []  # 2ecd
    duplicate_of: []  # 2ecd
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2ecd
    pr_ref:  # 2ecd
    description: "Per-pass records in `behavior_map.analysis_runs[]` carry `duration_ms` and `files_analyzed` fields meant to capture how much wall-clock and input each pass consumed. For passes that consume the in-memory IR rather than walking files (linkers and synthesis passes), both fields stay at zero — even when the pass executes for non-trivial wall-clock and emits substantial numbers of edges. The timer/counter update path is wired only on the file-walking branch.\n\n### Specific symptoms confirmed on hypergumbo self-analysis\n\n**(1) Eight synthesis-only passes report `files_analyzed=0` while running 71-4570 ms each.** Affected passes with their wall-clock durations: `pyffi-linker` (4570 ms), `di-resolution` (2550 ms), `method-call-recovery` (364 ms), `annotation-convention-linker` (247 ms), `containment-linker` (126 ms), `inherited-calls-linker` (71 ms), `inheritance-linker` (49 ms), `requirements` (42 ms). Total ~8 s of work is invisible to file-count throughput metrics. The `AnalysisRun.files_analyzed` field is initialized to 0 and never updated for these passes because they traverse the IR rather than files and have no natural file-counter.\n\n**(2) The pattern extends to 40 of 84 analysis_runs (not just the 8 worst offenders).** A broader scan finds 40 of 84 records with `files_analyzed=0` and `duration_ms>0`; total time consumed by file-less passes is ~7600 ms of 92,800 ms total (8.2% of analysis time has no file-level provenance). The synthesis/linker pass set is larger than the initial 8-pass observation suggested. The pattern is structural: every IR-consuming pass conflates \"pass did not run\" with \"pass ran on the graph.\"\n\n**(3) Several linker passes report `duration_ms=0` AND `files_analyzed=0` while emitting hundreds of edges.** Specific examples: `type-hierarchy` (duration=0 ms, emits 324 edges), `enclosure-linker` (duration=0 ms, emits 119 edges), `decorator-dispatch-linker` (duration=0 ms, emits 292 `dispatches_to` edges). Producing 324 edges in 0 ms is structurally impossible — the timer is not started for graph-consuming passes (or rounds down to 0 below 1 ms granularity). 17 of 84 runs have both `files=0` AND `duration=0`, yet several are credited with non-trivial edge production. The `duration_ms=0` failure compounds the `files_analyzed=0` failure to produce records that look like \"this pass did nothing\" despite real output.\n\n### Invariant\n\nEither every per-pass record should have an accurate `duration_ms` and a meaningful `files_analyzed` value, or a distinct provenance field should distinguish IR-consuming from file-walking passes so consumers can interpret `files_analyzed=0` correctly. Producing 324 edges in 0 ms must be impossible in well-formed provenance; the timer must start before the IR-consumption branch as well as before the file-walking branch.\n\n### Scope\n\nAffects roughly half of all per-pass records (40 of 84 on hypergumbo self-analysis report `files_analyzed=0`). A subset of those (17 of 84) also report `duration_ms=0`. Total invisible wall-clock from this pattern: ~8 s (~8% of analysis time).\n\n### Exposure\n\nBehavior-map per-pass provenance records, specifically `duration_ms` and `files_analyzed` fields on synthesis and linker passes; downstream consumers computing throughput, productivity, or timing metrics.\n\n### Consequence\n\nThroughput, productivity, and timing metrics computed from the provenance table misattribute IR-consuming work as free. Any analysis answering \"where did wall-clock time go\" or \"which passes are expensive\" gets a systematically wrong answer. Compounded with the `nodes_emitted` / `edges_emitted` gap on `AnalysisRun`, the IR-consuming pass set is essentially opaque at the provenance level.\n\n### Candidate fixes\n\n- Start the `duration_ms` timer at the entry point of every pass execution, not just the file-walking branch. Apply the same to `files_analyzed` initialization.\n- Add a distinct field (e.g., `ir_units_processed` or `pass_kind: file_walking | ir_consuming`) that lets consumers distinguish \"pass ran on graph\" from \"pass did not run.\" Rename `files_analyzed` if its semantics are file-walking-specific.\n- Add a property test that asserts no `AnalysisRun` with `nodes_emitted>0` or `edges_emitted>0` carries `duration_ms=0` — producing output in zero time is structurally impossible.\n- Document the IR-consuming-pass convention in the schema so consumers don't interpret `files_analyzed=0` as \"did not run.\"\n\n### Subsumed (do not chase)\n\nThis item subsumes INV-jifil, INV-viror, INV-vutat — which are deleted or will be deleted shortly and should only be referenced in an emergency."  # 2ecd
    fields:  # 2ecd
      dogfood_anon_id: "ITEM-54b776"  # 2ecd
      statement: "Either the timer and counter should start before the IR-consumption branch as well (so every pass has accurate timing), or a distinct provenance field should distinguish IR-consuming from file-walking passes so consumers can interpret `files_analyzed=0` correctly."  # 2ecd
      root_cause: "Per-pass records in the provenance table carry `duration_ms` and `files_analyzed` fields meant to capture how much wall-clock and input each pass consumed. For passes that consume the in-memory intermediate representation rather than walking files (such as linkers and synthesis passes), both fields are not updated and stay at zero — even when the pass executes for non-trivial duration and emits substantial numbers of edges. Several IR-consuming passes report `duration_ms=0` and `files_analyzed=0` while contributing hundreds of edges to the output. The pattern is consistent: the timer/counter update path is wired only on the file-walking branch."  # 2ecd
